From 5d5408a7552b392dc7897da24b7e62a779b14098 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Learning Garden <lab@example.org>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:47:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] lg_session: stop the fold work before freeing the session

Each session embeds a delayed work item that re-arms itself every 20 ms.
lg_session_release() frees the session while that work is still pending,
so the timer wheel keeps a pointer into freed memory. KASAN reports it
as soon as another timer is queued into the same bucket:

  BUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in enqueue_timer+0x9c/0x630
  Write of size 8 at addr ffff0000122aba50 by task stress-session./76
  ...
  Freed by task 76:
   kfree+0x150/0x600
   lg_session_release+0x94/0xd8 [lg_session]

Without KASAN the same bug shows up later and elsewhere: list corruption
in the timer code, a work function running on recycled memory, or a
crash after rmmod when the work fires in unloaded code.

Call cancel_delayed_work_sync() before the final fold and the kfree().
The _sync variant matters: the work re-arms itself, and only the _sync
variant both prevents the re-arm and waits for a running instance.

Signed-off-by: Learning Garden <lab@example.org>
---
 lg_session.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lg_session.c b/lg_session.c
index 1197a53..1096e9e 100644
--- a/lg_session.c
+++ b/lg_session.c
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@
  * what the session has collected into the global total, so a write never
  * touches the shared counter. Reading the device prints the total.
  *
- * Learning Garden, Kernel Engineering, Practical 2. This module has one bug.
+ * Learning Garden, Kernel Engineering, Practical 2. Reference fix applied.
  */
 #include <linux/atomic.h>
 #include <linux/fs.h>
@@ -76,6 +76,13 @@ static int lg_session_release(struct inode *inode, struct file *file)
 {
 	struct lg_session *s = file->private_data;
 
+	/*
+	 * The fold work re-arms itself, so it is always pending or running
+	 * while the session exists. Stop it and wait for it before the
+	 * memory that holds its timer goes away.
+	 */
+	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&s->fold);
+
 	/* Whatever the last fold has not seen yet still counts. */
 	atomic64_add(atomic64_xchg(&s->pending, 0), &lg_total);
 	kfree(s);
